**Theorem 108.4 (every repaired inverse, route and specified action
square).** Each of these four expressions recovers the other three on
its exact attained repair image, with both inverse identities. The same
holds after any fixed known number $n$ of actual subsequent passive
Tick;Hold pairs, retaining the samples at their original epoch. The
recovery maps commute with these actual passive steps and, at the odd
repair cut, with the particular performed use (107.2) on its declared
post-use image.

**Proof.** For $d=0$, Time and Boundary-plus recover
$\theta=2z$ in the fresh run or $\theta=-2y$ in the inherited run.
For $d>0$ use the same unique stacked rational solve as Theorem 107.1.
Space and Memory recover $\theta$ from the current $p_iR$ coordinates
at odd parity and $p_i$ at even parity. At the $d=k$ no-call image
the parity starts even. Conversely $\theta$ reconstructs the retained
$R\theta$, exactly the selected samples, their fixed performed chronology,
the actual current field, its metric/germ and the predictor component.
This proves both image identities individually for all four views,
including redundant rows of $R$, zero parameters and zero operands.
There are no unperformed samples in the re-encoding: it reconstructs
the contents of the specified already performed record.

Explicitly, let $\mathcal E_i^n(\theta)$ be one of these four
independently defined expressions and $\mathcal D_i^n$ its displayed
decoder. Then
$\mathcal D_i^n\mathcal E_i^n=\mathrm{Id}_{\mathbb Q^k}$ and
$\mathcal E_i^n\mathcal D_i^n=\mathrm{Id}$ on that image. A route
$i\to j$ is $\mathcal E_j^n\mathcal D_i^n$; composing any two routes
gives the direct route. Equality of each view is $\theta$ equality,
hence exactly the full-current-service kernel in this fixed context.

One actual Tick;Hold updates the field by $B$, increments the retained
count and appends precisely those real calls to Time. Boundary-plus
keeps its old measured samples and recomputes the *present* germ with
paid work; Memory updates its actual predictor. Since $B^2H=H$,
each expression becomes $\mathcal E_i^{n+1}(\theta)$. Both orders of
transport and recovery therefore give $\mathcal E_j^{n+1}(\theta)$.
This algebra verifies the real updates just specified, rather than
defining the observations by desired inverses.

For (107.2), Time appends the actual Add/Hold/Read and literal $q$;
Boundary-plus retains the repair samples and exposes the updated germ
$OGBH\theta$; Space and Memory expose $GBH\theta$. The unchanged
$p_iR$ values still decode $\theta$ (or first apply $G^{-1}$).
Re-encoding gives exactly these post-use contents, so the same two
image identities and the before/after action square hold. No passive
image after an arbitrary later control is assumed. $\square$

